   $q$What is the author's main purpose in this essay?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To persuade students to limit notifications and, as future designers, to build apps that respect attention","is_correct":true},{"text":"To warn readers that shopping apps are the only kind that send unnecessary alerts","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"To argue that teenagers should stop using phones entirely while doing their homework","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates-claim"},{"text":"To explain the programming steps a designer follows to add notifications to a new app","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To persuade students to limit notifications and, as future designers, to build apps that respect attention$q$, $q$She challenges readers to switch off unneeded notifications and ends by urging future designers to "build apps that respect the people who use them." She never says to stop using phones, so that choice overstates her claim.$q$, 'draft', 'ee5f3edf-399d-5092-a219-43ac8edf1a97')
