   $q$Which statement best describes how the author handles the argument about translation apps?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He mocks the people who use apps, then argues that phones should not be allowed in language classrooms.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"He dismisses it without discussion, then gives statistics showing how often translation apps make errors.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"He calls it \"a fair question,\" then answers with cultural and personal experiences that an app cannot provide.","is_correct":true},{"text":"He agrees with it completely, then suggests that students use apps instead of taking a third year of class.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-viewpoint"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He calls it "a fair question," then answers with cultural and personal experiences that an app cannot provide.$q$, $q$He concedes "It is a fair question" and then lists things an app cannot do, such as explaining jokes or politeness, or giving the feeling of a stranger's face lighting up. He offers no statistics and does not dismiss the question.$q$, 'draft', 'f863236c-afb5-59f4-b253-59d685a12316')
