  ('afb1c377-911f-5d37-8eb1-8aa9ae818988', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-authors-purpose'), null, 'hard',
   $q$How do the essay's opening and closing work together to advance the author's purpose?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The opening and closing both describe vultures in the desert, showing that the essay is mainly about desert ecology.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"The opening and closing both use scientific data, showing that the author relies only on logic rather than emotion.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-evidence"},{"text":"The opening shows circling vultures as a cartoon sign of trouble, and the closing recasts that same image as a dedicated worker.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The opening praises vultures as helpful workers, and the closing admits that most people will never accept that view.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The opening shows circling vultures as a cartoon sign of trouble, and the closing recasts that same image as a dedicated worker.$q$, $q$The essay starts with vultures that "circle over lost travelers" in cartoons and ends with "a dark shape circling high above the ridge" that is really "one of nature's most dedicated workers." The opening presents the negative view; it does not praise vultures.$q$, 'draft', '99e804a9-6100-51fa-b6d6-fb4fef3eb4f3')
on conflict (id) do update set
